---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import { SITE } from "../config";
const updated = "5 July 2026";
---

<Base
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms that govern the kirpik.app website and the Kirpik text protection app for Shopify, operated by INFOWISE LIMITED."
>
  <PageHero title="Terms of Service" />

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0">
    <div class="container narrow prose">
      <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> {updated}</p>
      <p>
        These terms govern your use of the Kirpik text protection app for
        Shopify and of this website, both operated by {SITE.developer}
        ("Kirpik", "we", "us"). By installing or using the app, or using this
        site, you agree to them.
      </p>

      <h2>The service</h2>
      <p>
        Kirpik embeds invisible watermarks in the Shopify text content you
        choose to protect: product descriptions, blog articles and pages. It
        lets you detect those watermarks in pasted text or at URLs you supply,
        and generates Chain of Proof certificates from confirmed detections.
        Features, content limits, URL check allowances and certificate
        allowances depend on your plan.
      </p>

      <h2>Your responsibilities</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>You must own, or hold the necessary rights to, the content you protect and the text you check with Kirpik.</li>
        <li>You are responsible for the accuracy of any takedown notice or complaint you send, and for how you use Chain of Proof certificates.</li>
        <li>You must use the app and this site lawfully and in line with Shopify's terms.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Plans and billing</h2>
      <p>
        Paid plans are billed in USD through Shopify Managed Pricing and
        appear on your Shopify invoice. You can change or cancel your plan at
        any time from the app or your Shopify admin. Protection is reversible:
        if a downgrade puts you over the new plan's limits, the most recently
        protected items above the cap are restored to their unprotected state.
      </p>

      <h2>No legal advice, no promised outcomes</h2>
      <p>
        Kirpik provides tooling and evidence. It does not provide legal
        advice, and nothing on this site is legal advice. We cannot promise
        that any host, marketplace, search engine or other third party will
        act on a notice, remove content or accept a certificate, since those
        decisions belong to them.
      </p>

      <h2>Fair use of the service</h2>
      <p>
        Detection allowances and content limits exist to keep the service fast
        and affordable for everyone. We may throttle or suspend accounts that
        attempt to probe, reverse engineer or abuse the watermarking or
        detection systems, or that use detection against content they have no
        legitimate interest in.
      </p>

      <h2>Warranty and liability</h2>
      <p>
        The service is provided on an "as is" basis. To the maximum extent
        permitted by law, we exclude implied warranties and are not liable for
        indirect or consequential loss arising from use of the app or this
        website.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        We may update these terms from time to time. The date above shows the
        current version. Continued use of the app or site after changes take
        effect constitutes acceptance of the revised terms.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about these terms go to {SITE.developer} at
        <a href="mailto:support@kirpik.app">support@kirpik.app</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
